@startuml
title CargoWise eAdaptor Next - Inbound and Outbound Mechanism

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

actor "External System\n(Client / Boomi / ERP)" as EXT
actor "CargoWise User" as USER

rectangle "CargoWise UAT Environment" as CW {
  
  component "CargoWise Business Object\nShipment / Org / Invoice / Milestone" as OBJ
  
  rectangle "eAdaptor Next" as EAN {
    component "Inbound Path" as IN
    component "Outbound Path" as OUT
    component "Authentication\nBasic Auth / Token" as AUTH
    component "Message Validation\nXML / XSD / Schema" as VALID
    component "Message Queue" as QUEUE
    component "Processing Engine" as ENGINE
    component "Message Logs\nSuccess / Error / Retry" as LOG
  }
}

database "CargoWise Database" as DB

rectangle "Middleware Layer\nBoomi / API Gateway" as MW
cloud "Client Endpoint\nAPI / SFTP / Web Service" as CLIENT

'========================
' INBOUND FLOW
'========================
EXT --> AUTH : 1. Send inbound request\nHTTP POST / SOAP / SFTP\nwith credentials
AUTH --> IN : 2. Authentication passed
IN --> VALID : 3. Validate payload\nXML / schema / mandatory fields
VALID --> QUEUE : 4. Accepted message queued
QUEUE --> ENGINE : 5. Process inbound message
ENGINE --> OBJ : 6. Create / update CW object
OBJ --> DB : 7. Save transaction
ENGINE --> LOG : 8. Write processing result
LOG --> EXT : 9. Return response\nSuccess / Error

'========================
' OUTBOUND FLOW
'========================
USER --> OBJ : 1. User updates CW data\nShipment / Milestone / Invoice
OBJ --> OUT : 2. Event trigger activated
OUT --> VALID : 3. Build outbound XML payload
VALID --> QUEUE : 4. Queue outbound message
QUEUE --> MW : 5. Send message to middleware
MW --> CLIENT : 6. Transform / route to client endpoint
CLIENT --> MW : 7. Response / acknowledgement
MW --> LOG : 8. Return status to CW
LOG --> USER : 9. Admin checks success/error log

note right of AUTH
Inbound requires valid
endpoint + credential +
permission setup.
end note

note right of VALID
Schema validation checks:
- XML format
- mandatory fields
- data structure
- message type
end note

note bottom of LOG
Logs are used for:
- troubleshooting
- retry
- audit trail
- support analysis
end note

@enduml